                  SECTION 2: STACK OPERATIONS & TERMINOLOGY
===============================================================================

🔹 BASIC STACK OPERATIONS:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. PUSH (Insert)
   ├─ Adds an element to the TOP of the stack
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Can cause Stack Overflow if stack is full

2. POP (Delete)
   ├─ Removes and returns the TOP element
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Can cause Stack Underflow if stack is empty

3. PEEK/TOP (Access)
   ├─ Returns the TOP element WITHOUT removing it
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Useful for checking what's on top

4. isEmpty()
   ├─ Checks if stack is empty
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Returns true if no elements, false otherwise

5. isFull()
   ├─ Checks if stack is full (for array implementation)
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Only relevant for fixed-size arrays

6. size()
   ├─ Returns number of elements in stack
   ├─ Time Complexity: O(1)
   └─ Useful for knowing current stack size

🔹 STACK TERMINOLOGY:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

• TOP/TOS (Top of Stack): Pointer to the topmost element
• CAPACITY: Maximum number of elements stack can hold
• SIZE: Current number of elements in stack
• STACK OVERFLOW: Trying to push when stack is full
• STACK UNDERFLOW: Trying to pop when stack is empty

🔹 VISUAL REPRESENTATION:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Empty Stack:        After push(10):     After push(20):     After pop():
                                                            
                        top → [20]         top → [30]         top → [20]
                              [10]               [20]               [10]
    top → [ ]               [ ]                [10]               [ ]
          [ ]               [ ]                [ ]                [ ]
          [ ]               [ ]                [ ]                [ ]

Operations Flow:
push(10) → push(20) → push(30) → pop() returns 30 → push(40) → peek() returns 40

