           SECTION 8: STACK OVERFLOW & UNDERFLOW HANDLING
===============================================================================

🔹 STACK OVERFLOW:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Occurs when: Trying to push element into full stack

Causes:
• Stack size is fixed (array implementation)
• Too many push operations without pop
• Infinite recursion (function calls)

Solutions:
1. Check isFull() before pushing
2. Use dynamic array (ArrayList in Java)
3. Implement using linked list
4. Increase initial capacity

Prevention Code:
```java
public void push(int x) {
    if (isFull()) {
        // Option 1: Return error
        throw new StackOverflowError("Stack is full");
        
        // Option 2: Resize array (dynamic stack)
        resize(2 * capacity);
    }
    arr[++top] = x;
}
```

🔹 STACK UNDERFLOW:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Occurs when: Trying to pop element from empty stack

Causes:
• More pop operations than push
• Popping without checking if empty

Solutions:
1. Always check isEmpty() before pop
2. Handle gracefully with return value or exception

Prevention Code:
```java
public int pop() {
    if (isEmpty()) {
        // Option 1: Return sentinel value
        return Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        
        // Option 2: Throw exception
        throw new EmptyStackException();
    }
    return arr[top--];
}
```

