🔹 STACK vs QUEUE:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
│ Feature          │ Stack           │ Queue               │
├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ Principle        │ LIFO            │ FIFO                │
│ Insertion        │ Top only        │ Rear only           │
│ Deletion         │ Top only        │ Front only          │
│ Access Points    │ One (top)       │ Two (front & rear)  │
│ Real-world       │ Plates stack    │ Ticket line         │
│ Used in          │ Recursion, DFS  │ BFS, Scheduling     │
└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

🔹 WHEN TO USE STACK:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Use Stack when:
✅ Need LIFO behavior
✅ Implementing recursion iteratively
✅ Backtracking problems
✅ Parsing expressions
✅ Checking balanced symbols
✅ Undo/Redo operations
✅ DFS traversal

Don't use Stack when:
❌ Need FIFO behavior (use Queue)
❌ Need random access (use Array)
❌ Need priority-based access (use Priority Queue)

