───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. Stack follows LIFO (Last In First Out) principle
2. All basic operations are O(1) time complexity
3. Array implementation has fixed size limitation
4. Always check isEmpty() before pop/peek
5. Always check isFull() before push (in array)
6. top = -1 indicates empty stack
7. Space complexity is O(n) where n is capacity

🔹 COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

❌ Forgetting to check isEmpty() before pop → Stack Underflow
❌ Forgetting to check isFull() before push → Stack Overflow
❌ Using wrong index (top vs top+1)
❌ Not initializing top = -1
❌ Confusing LIFO with FIFO
❌ Not handling edge cases in problems

